IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part II -- Provisions applicable to Acts, ss 6 to 13.
-- Ss 10A(3), 10A(4), 11 and 12 are time rules and live in vic-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part II -- Provisions applicable to Acts`

§§ `s 6 Construction of Acts`

DECLARE VicEffectOfAProvisionAgainstTheLimitOfPower IS ONE OF
    VicOperatesFully
    VicOperatesToTheExtentNotInExcessAndTheRemainderIsNotAffected

-- s 6(1): an Act is construed as operating to the full extent of, but not exceeding, the legislative power of Victoria; a provision (or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance) that would otherwise be in excess of that power operates to the extent it is not in excess, and the remainder of the Act and the application of that provision to others is not affected.
-- src:55 | (1) Every Act shall be construed as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the legislative power of the State of Victoria, to the intent that where a provision of an Act, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of that power, it shall nevertheless be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power and the remainder of the Act and the application of that provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances shall not be affected.
@ref s 6(1) (src:55)
GIVEN wouldOtherwiseBeInExcessOfThatPower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A VicEffectOfAProvisionAgainstTheLimitOfPower
`s6(1) how a provision of an Act is construed against the limit of the legislative power of Victoria` MEANS
    IF wouldOtherwiseBeInExcessOfThatPower
    THEN VicOperatesToTheExtentNotInExcessAndTheRemainderIsNotAffected
    ELSE VicOperatesFully

-- s 6(2): the section is in addition to, and not in derogation of, any provision of an Act on the construction or extent of operation of that Act.
-- src:56 | (2) The provisions of this section are in addition to, and not in derogation of, any provision of any Act relating to the construction, or extent of the operation, of that Act.
@ref s 6(2) (src:56)
GIVEN anotherProvisionOfThatActOnConstructionOrExtentOfOperation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s6(2) s 6 takes the place of a provision of the Act on its construction or extent of operation` MEANS
    IF anotherProvisionOfThatActOnConstructionOrExtentOfOperation THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 7 Sections to be substantive enactments`

-- s 7: every section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
-- src:58 | 7 Sections to be substantive enactments
-- src:59 | Every section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
@ref s 7 (src:58-59)
GIVEN sectionHasIntroductoryWords IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s7 a section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment` MEANS
    JUST TRUE

§§ `s 8 Amendment or repeal in same session`

-- s 8: an Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it is passed.
-- src:61 | 8 Amendment or repeal in same session
-- src:62 | An Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it is passed.
@ref s 8 (src:61-62)
GIVEN sameSessionAsPassing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s8 an Act may be amended or repealed in the session` MEANS
    IF sameSessionAsPassing THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 9 Citation of Acts by number`

-- s 9(1): the Acts passed in a calendar year are numbered in a regular arithmetical series, beginning with 1, in the order in which they receive (or are deemed to receive) the Royal Assent.
-- src:66 | (1) The Acts passed in each calendar year shall be numbered in regular arithmetical series, beginning with the number 1, in the order in which they receive or, for the purposes of section 69 of the Constitution Act 1975, are deemed to have received the Royal Assent.
@ref s 9(1) (src:66)
GIVEN actsAlreadyAssentedToInThatCalendarYear IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s9(1) number of an Act among the Acts of its calendar year` MEANS
    actsAlreadyAssentedToInThatCalendarYear PLUS 1

-- s 9(2): it is sufficient to refer to an Act by the number of that Act only if it was passed before 1 January 1986, and by the calendar year and its number among that year's Acts if it was passed on or after 1 January 1986.
-- src:67 | (2) It is sufficient to refer to an Act in—
-- src:68 | (a) any other Act;
-- src:69 | (b) a subordinate instrument;
-- src:70 | (c) a deed or other instrument; or
-- src:71 | (d) any other document whatsoever—
-- src:72 | by—
-- src:73 | (e) in the case of an Act passed before 1 January 1986, the number of that Act only; and
-- src:74 | (f) in the case of an Act passed on or after 1 January 1986, the calendar year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year.
@ref s 9(2) (src:67-74)
GIVEN passedOn IS A DATE, citedByNumberOnly IS A BOOLEAN, citedByYearAndNumber IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s9(2) the way of referring to an Act is sufficient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF passedOn AT MOST `s9(2)(e) last day of the period in which an Act is cited by its number only` AND citedByNumberOnly THEN JUST TRUE
        IF passedOn AT LEAST `s9(2)(f) first day of the period in which an Act is cited by year and number` AND citedByYearAndNumber THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 9(3): a failure to comply with subsection (1) in a calendar year does not affect the operation or effect of an Act passed in that year.
-- src:76 | (3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) in a calendar year (whether the calendar year 2006 or any earlier or later calendar year) does not affect the validity, operation or effect of an Act passed in that year.
@ref s 9(3) (src:76)
GIVEN failedToNumberInARegularSeries IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s9(3) a failure to number the Acts of a year in a regular series affects the operation or effect of an Act passed that year` MEANS
    IF failedToNumberInARegularSeries THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 10 Citation of Acts by title`

DECLARE VicFormOfCitationOfAnAct IS ONE OF
    VicByTheShortTitleTheActAuthorises
    VicByTheTitleBeforeTheEnactingWordsOrPreamble

-- s 10(1): an Act may be cited by the short title it authorises or, if it authorises none, by the title appearing before the enacting words (or before the preamble).
-- src:80 | (1) An Act may be cited in—
-- src:81 | (a) that Act or any other Act;
-- src:82 | (b) a subordinate instrument;
-- src:83 | (c) a deed or other instrument;
-- src:84 | (d) any other document whatsoever—
-- src:85 | by—
-- src:86 | (e) the short title authorized by that Act whether or not that Act or the provision of that Act authorizing that form of citation has come into operation or has been repealed; or
-- src:87 | (f) if there is no short title authorized by that Act, the title appearing before the enacting words or, if there is a preamble, before the preamble, whether or not that Act has come into operation or has been repealed.
@ref s 10(1) (src:80-87)
GIVEN actAuthorisesAShortTitle IS A BOOLEAN, form IS A VicFormOfCitationOfAnAct
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10(1) this section permits citing the Act in that form` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN VicByTheShortTitleTheActAuthorises THEN IF actAuthorisesAShortTitle THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN VicByTheTitleBeforeTheEnactingWordsOrPreamble THEN IF actAuthorisesAShortTitle THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 10(2): the title appearing before the enacting words (or the preamble) forms part of the Act if there is no short title authorized by the Act.
-- src:88 | (2) The title of an Act appearing before the enacting words or, if there is a preamble, before the preamble, forms part of the Act if there is no short title authorized by the Act.
@ref s 10(2) (src:88)
GIVEN actAuthorisesAShortTitle IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10(2) the title before the enacting words forms part of the Act` MEANS
    IF actAuthorisesAShortTitle THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 10(2AA): a citation by that title that is in italics without bolding is sufficient for subsection (1).
-- src:90 | (2AA) A citation of an Act by the title appearing before the enacting words or, if there is a preamble, before the preamble, being a citation that is in italics without bolding, is sufficient for the purposes of subsection (1).
@ref s 10(2AA) (src:90)
GIVEN inItalics IS A BOOLEAN, inBold IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10(2AA) a citation by the title is sufficient for s 10(1)` MEANS
    IF inItalics AND NOT (inBold) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10(2A): the Clerk of the Parliaments must alter the title of a Bill to be presented for the Royal Assent by substituting the word "Act" for the word "Bill".
-- src:92 | (2A) The Clerk of the Parliaments must alter the title appearing before the enacting words (or, if there is a preamble, before the preamble) in a Bill that is to be presented to the Governor for the Royal Assent by substituting the word "Act" for the word "Bill".
@ref s 10(2A) (src:92)
GIVEN billToBePresentedForRoyalAssent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s10(2A) word the Clerk of the Parliaments substitutes for the word Bill in the title` MEANS
    IF billToBePresentedForRoyalAssent THEN JUST "Act" ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10(2B): the alteration is not to be taken to be an amendment of the Bill.
-- src:94 | (2B) The alteration of a Bill to give effect to subsection (2A) is not to be taken to be an amendment of the Bill.
@ref s 10(2B) (src:94)
GIVEN alterationMadeUnderSubsection2A IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10(2B) the alteration to give effect to s 10(2A) is an amendment of the Bill` MEANS
    IF alterationMadeUnderSubsection2A THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10(3): if an Act passed on or after 1 September 1985 does not authorize its citation by a short title, the long title of the Bill does not form part of the Act.
-- src:95 | (3) If an Act passed on or after 1 September 1985 does not authorize its citation by a short title, the long title of the Bill for the Act does not form part of the Act.
@ref s 10(3) (src:95)
GIVEN passedOn IS A DATE, actAuthorisesAShortTitle IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10(3) the long title of the Bill forms part of the Act` MEANS
    IF passedOn AT LEAST `s10(3) first day on which an Act passed without a short title leaves its long title out of the Act` AND NOT (actAuthorisesAShortTitle)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 10A Construction of power to fix commencement of Act`

-- s 10A(1): an Act providing for the Act or a provision to come into operation on a day to be proclaimed confers power on the Governor in Council to fix, by proclamation published in the Government Gazette, a day for it to come into operation.
-- src:99 | (1) If an Act provides for the Act or a provision of the Act to come into operation on a day to be proclaimed, the Act confers power on the Governor in Council to fix by proclamation published in the Government Gazette a day for the Act or provision to come into operation.
@ref s 10A(1) (src:99)
GIVEN providesForADayToBeProclaimed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10A(1) the Act confers power on the Governor in Council to fix a day by proclamation` MEANS
    IF providesForADayToBeProclaimed THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 10A(2): an Act providing for a day or days to be proclaimed confers power to fix a day for the Act or provisions or different days for different provisions.
-- src:100 | (2) If an Act provides for the Act or provisions of the Act to come into operation on a day or days to be proclaimed, the Act confers power on the Governor in Council to fix by proclamation or proclamations published in the Government Gazette—
-- src:101 | (a) a day for the Act or provisions to come into operation; or
-- src:102 | (b) different days for different provisions of the Act to come into operation.
@ref s 10A(2) (src:100-102)
GIVEN providesForADayOrDaysToBeProclaimed IS A BOOLEAN, wantsDifferentDaysForDifferentProvisions IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s10A(2) the Act confers power to fix the days by proclamation in that way` MEANS
    IF providesForADayOrDaysToBeProclaimed THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 13 Exercise of powers between passing and commencement of Act`

-- s 13(1): the section applies where an Act or provision not in operation on passing will, on coming into operation, confer power (or amend another Act to confer power) to make instruments, give notices, make appointments, establish a body, prescribe forms or do any other thing for the purposes of that Act or provision.
-- src:125 | (1) This section applies where an Act or a provision of an Act which does not come into operation immediately on the passing of the Act will, on its coming into operation, confer power or amend another Act so as to confer power under the other Act as so amended to—
-- src:126 | (a) make subordinate instruments or any other instruments of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:127 | (b) give notices; or
-- src:128 | (c) make appointments; or
-- src:129 | (d) establish a body; or
-- src:130 | (e) prescribe forms; or
-- src:131 | (f) do any other thing—
-- src:132 | for the purposes of that Act or provision or that other Act.
@ref s 13(1) (src:125-132)
GIVEN doesNotComeIntoOperationOnPassing IS A BOOLEAN, willConferPowerOnComingIntoOperation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s13(1) s 13 applies` MEANS
    IF doesNotComeIntoOperationOnPassing AND willConferPowerOnComingIntoOperation THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 13(2): unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act.
-- src:133 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act but its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation on a person before the coming into operation of the Act or provision except insofar as is necessary or expedient for the purpose of—
-- src:134 | (a) bringing the Act or provision into operation; or
-- src:135 | (b) making the Act or provision or the other Act as amended fully effective at or after that coming into operation.
@ref s 13(2) (src:133-135)
GIVEN section13Applies IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s13(2) the power may be exercised after the passing and before the commencement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT section13Applies THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 13(2): its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation on a person before the coming into operation, except insofar as necessary or expedient to bring the Act or provision into operation or to make it fully effective at or after that coming into operation.
-- src:133 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act but its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation on a person before the coming into operation of the Act or provision except insofar as is necessary or expedient for the purpose of—
-- src:134 | (a) bringing the Act or provision into operation; or
-- src:135 | (b) making the Act or provision or the other Act as amended fully effective at or after that coming into operation.
@ref s 13(2) (src:133-135)
GIVEN section13Applies IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, necessaryOrExpedientToBringIntoOperation IS A BOOLEAN, necessaryOrExpedientToMakeFullyEffective IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s13(2) the exercise of the power confers a right or imposes an obligation before the commencement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT section13Applies THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        IF necessaryOrExpedientToBringIntoOperation OR necessaryOrExpedientToMakeFullyEffective THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 13(3): without limiting subsection (2), an appointee may exercise a power, and a body may meet and exercise a power, before the coming into operation as if the Act or provision were in operation, with the same entitlement to remuneration or allowances.
-- src:136 | (3) Without limiting subsection (2), an appointee may exercise a power, and a body may meet and exercise a power, under that subsection before the coming into operation of the Act or provision in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations (if any) and with an entitlement to payment of the same remuneration or allowances (if any) as if the Act or provision were in operation.
@ref s 13(3) (src:136)
GIVEN section13Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s13(3) an appointee or body may exercise the power before the commencement as if the Act were in operation` MEANS
    IF section13Applies THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 13(4): for a provision on the duration of a term of office, the term does not begin until the Act or provision comes into operation, despite the exercise of a power under the section before then.
-- src:137 | (4) For the purposes of any provision as to the duration of the term of office of an appointee (including a member of a body), that term does not begin until the coming into operation of the Act or provision despite the exercise of any power under this section before that coming into operation.
@ref s 13(4) (src:137)
GIVEN dayOfQuestion IS A DATE, dayActOrProvisionComesIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s13(4) the term of office cannot yet begin` MEANS
    IF dayOfQuestion LESS THAN dayActOrProvisionComesIntoOperation THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
